   "evidence": "The proof uses `Finite \u03c3` only via `Fintype.ofFinite \u03c3` for `Fintype.card \u03c3` (line 142) and `Finset.univ.filter (i < \u00b7)` (line 143), both bounded quantities over variables that occur in some `v \u2208 V`; `Mathlib/RingTheory/MvPowerSeries/LexOrder.lean:30` assumes only `[LinearOrder \u03c3] [WellFoundedGT \u03c3]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/MvPolynomial/LazardValuation.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `[Finite \u03c3]`. Replace `Finset.univ` by `S := hV.toFinset.biUnion Finsupp.support` (finite, since `V` is finite and each `v` has finite support): set `rk i := (S.filter (i < \u00b7)).card` and `M := S.card * K + 1`. The calc is unchanged \u2014 `weight_eq_sum` sums over `(v.filter (i < \u00b7)).support \u2286 v.support \u2286 S`, so at most `S.card` terms contribute, each `\u2264 K * M ^ (rk i - 1)`, and `hrk` holds for `j \u2208 S`, `i < j`.",
   "issue": "`exists_isLazardEvaluator` assumes `[Finite \u03c3]`, but only `V.Finite` is needed; `\u03c3` may be infinite with `WellFoundedGT` (e.g. `\u2115\u1d52\u1d48`), and the module docstring then overstates the hypothesis as \"in finitely many variables\".",
   "line": "135"
  },
  {
   "evidence": "`Set.finite_Iic D` needs only `LocallyFiniteOrderBot (\u03c3 \u2192\u2080 \u2115)`, available for arbitrary `\u03c3` from `Finsupp.instLocallyFiniteOrder` (`Mathlib/Data/Finsupp/Interval.lean:85`, hypotheses `[PartialOrder \u03b1] [Zero \u03b1] [LocallyFiniteOrder \u03b1] [DecidableEq \u03b9] [DecidableEq \u03b1]`) plus `Finsupp.orderBot` (`Mathlib/Data/Finsupp/Order.lean:218`) through `LocallyFiniteOrder.toLocallyFiniteOrderTop`'s `to_dual` (`Mathlib/Order/Interval/Finset/Defs.lean:402`); `Multiset.toFinsupp_apply` is `Mathlib/Data/Finsupp/Multiset.lean:152`, `degreeOf_def` is `Mathlib/Algebra/MvPolynomial/Degrees.lean:220`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/MvPolynomial/LazardValuation.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `[Finite \u03c3]` and build `D` without `Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite`: `D := p.degrees.toFinsupp`, which satisfies `D i = p.degreeOf i` by `Multiset.toFinsupp_apply` and `degreeOf_def`. The rest of the proof is unchanged.",
   "issue": "`finite_range_lazardValuation` assumes `[Finite \u03c3]`, but the bound `v i \u2264 p.degreeOf i` already forces `v.support \u2286 p.vars`, so the range is finite for any `\u03c3`.",
